## Using Custom Components

This guide covers all available Markdoc components.

### Callouts

Use callouts to highlight important information:

{% Callout type="info" %}
This is an info callout for general information.
{% /Callout %}

{% Callout type="warning" title="Be Careful" %}
This is a warning callout.
{% /Callout %}

{% Callout type="danger" title="Important" %}
This is a danger callout for critical information.
{% /Callout %}

{% Callout type="quote" %}
This is a quote block for citations and references.
{% /Callout %}

### Video Embeds

Embed videos from YouTube, Vimeo, or self-hosted sources using the VideoEmbed component in the editor.

### Image Blocks

Place images with different positions:

- **center** — centered with max width
- **full-width** — spans the full content width
- **left** — floats left with text wrapping
- **right** — floats right with text wrapping

### Image Gallery

Group images side by side using the ImageGallery wrapper component.

## Markdown Basics

Standard Markdown still works:

- **Bold** and *italic* text
- [Links](https://example.com)
- Lists (ordered and unordered)
- Code blocks with syntax highlighting
- Tables
- Headings (H2 through H5)
